<title>UK: Commerzbank sets warrants on German government bonds. [CORRECTED 10:47 gmt]</title>
<headline>Commerzbank sets warrants on German government bonds. [CORRECTED 10:47 gmt]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects headline from &quot;government indices&quot;)</p>
<p>Commerzbank AG  has issued 10 million American-style put warrants, in four equal tranches, on the 6.0 pct Bundesanleihe due 2007, the 6.25 pct Bundesanleihe due 2024 and the DTB Bund Future, lead manager Commerz Financial Products said.</p>
<p>One warrant controls one share.</p>
<p> WARRANTS	STRIKE	  ISS PRICE	MATURITY</p>
<p>DTB BUND FUTURE</p>
<p> PUT	     102.07 PCT    1.20 DEM	 15.JUL.97</p>
<p>6.0  PCT    BUND 2007</p>
<p> PUT	     102.00 PCT    3.05 DEM	 23.JAN.98</p>
<p>6.25 PCT BUND 2024</p>
<p> PUT		94.00 PCT    2.00 DEM	 15.OCT.97</p>
<p> PUT		96.00 PCT    2.86 DEM	 15.OCT.97</p>
<p> PAYDATE	19.FEB.97		    LISTING   FFT DDF</p>
<p>--Reuter London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
